{
  "uid": "vpay-rails",
  "title": "vpay: rails, charges and webhooks",
  "description": "Calls to the payment rails, the charge state machine, provider callbacks and the webhook delivery backlog. Counts calls to whatever host a rail is configured with: it does not say a rail works. Generated by tools/dashboards/rails.py.",
  "tags": [
    "vpay"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "timezone": "utc",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "job",
        "label": "Service",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(vpay_build_info, job)",
          "refId": "job"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(vpay_build_info, job)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What a rail panel does and does not say",
      "description": "A note for the reader of this dashboard.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**These panels count calls vpay made to the host a rail is configured with, and what came back.** A rail configured against a stub host (a WireMock container in the dev, demo and end-to-end stacks) reports exactly like a live one, and a rail whose adapter is not written reports its `not_implemented` error here. Nothing on this dashboard says a rail *works*: `docs/status.md` says which rails have been called live, and when. The calls are port calls, not wire requests (`docs/reference/vpay-core.md`)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Rail calls",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rail calls by provider and operation",
      "description": "Calls per second to each rail, by port operation (prepare, submit, query_status, refund, account_holder_name, ensure_callback_endpoint).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (provider, operation) (rate(vpay_provider_requests_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} {{operation}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rail call errors by provider and kind",
      "description": "Calls that failed, per second, by rail and by error code (the same words as provider_requests.error_kind). not_implemented is an adapter that does not do this yet, not an outage.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (provider, error_kind) (rate(vpay_provider_requests_total{job=~\"$job\",error_kind!=\"\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} {{error_kind}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rail call error ratio by provider",
      "description": "The share of each rail's calls that failed. A rail with a handful of calls has a ratio that jumps on one failure; read it with the rate above.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (provider) (rate(vpay_provider_requests_total{job=~\"$job\",error_kind!=\"\"}[$__rate_interval])) / sum by (provider) (rate(vpay_provider_requests_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rail call latency by provider (p50, p95, p99)",
      "description": "Wall-clock time of one call to a rail, per provider. Mobile-money rails are slow in a way an HTTP route is not.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le, provider) (rate(vpay_provider_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} p50",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, provider) (rate(vpay_provider_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} p95",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, provider) (rate(vpay_provider_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} p99",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Charges",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Charge transitions by new state",
      "description": "Charges entering each state per second, by rail. A charge is the unit that moves through submitting, submitted, pending, unresolved, succeeded and failed; the payment intent's own status is not exported (it has no index to count by).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (provider, to) (rate(vpay_charge_transitions_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} -> {{to}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 40,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Charge transitions (from, to)",
      "description": "Each edge of the charge state machine per second. The edge is the alertable quantity: submitted to failed is a decline, pending to unresolved is a poll ladder that ran out.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 22,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (from, to) (rate(vpay_charge_transitions_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{from}} -> {{to}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Charges that went unresolved in the range",
      "description": "Charges whose poll ladder ended with no answer from the rail. Each one needs a human: orange at one.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(vpay_charge_transitions_total{job=~\"$job\",to=\"unresolved\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 10
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Charges that failed in the range",
      "description": "Charges that ended failed: a rail declining or an error. Read with the error panels above; a payer who declines is not an incident.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 30,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(vpay_charge_transitions_total{job=~\"$job\",to=\"failed\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Provider callbacks by verdict",
      "description": "Callbacks received for a charge vpay holds, by what the rail's check said. invalid is a wrong signature (a misconfigured secret, or a forgery); no_secret is a rail that signs and a deployment with no secret set; not_checked is a rail whose callbacks vpay does not check.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 30,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (provider, verdict) (rate(vpay_provider_callbacks_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} {{verdict}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Webhooks to merchants",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 38,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Webhook backlog",
      "description": "Deliveries owed an attempt (state pending). It includes deliveries waiting for a retry rung that is not due yet, so it is a size, not a lateness: read it with the overdue age beside it. Orange at 1,000, red at 10,000.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(vpay_webhook_deliveries_pending{job=~\"$job\"})",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1000
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 10000
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Oldest overdue delivery",
      "description": "How long the most overdue pending delivery is past its next attempt; zero when none is due. A value that keeps growing is a worker that is not delivering. Orange at 5 minutes, red at 30.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 39,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(vpay_webhook_oldest_pending_overdue_seconds{job=~\"$job\"})",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 300
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1800
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Webhook backlog over time",
      "description": "The two backlog numbers together: a burst rises and falls, a stalled worker rises with the overdue age.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 39,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(vpay_webhook_deliveries_pending{job=~\"$job\"})",
          "legendFormat": "pending deliveries",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "max(vpay_webhook_oldest_pending_overdue_seconds{job=~\"$job\"})",
          "legendFormat": "oldest overdue (s)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Webhook delivery attempts by outcome",
      "description": "Delivery attempts per second as succeeded, retry (the ladder has a rung left) or exhausted (parked for a human, docs/runbooks/webhook-delivery-failures.md).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 44,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(vpay_webhook_deliveries_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 40,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Deliveries exhausted in the range",
      "description": "Deliveries whose retry ladder ran out. Each one is a merchant who did not get an event and needs a person: orange at one.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 47,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(vpay_webhook_deliveries_total{job=~\"$job\",outcome=\"exhausted\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 10
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Account-holder lookups by outcome",
      "description": "GET /v1/account_holders answers per second: found, not_found, unsupported (no rail could answer) and error (a rail or a malformed number). No label carries the number or the name.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 52,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(vpay_account_holder_lookups_total{job=~\"$job\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
